  "question": {
    "text": "A metallic cube of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> moving along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at a uniform velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. In a region of uniform magnetic field of magnitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> directed along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>- axis. In equilibrium the potential difference between the faces of higher and lower potential developed because of the motion through the field will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mV</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0042_c1df3327df95.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 301px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using the equation</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>Using the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi></math></p>"
  }
